# Milestone: v0.13.3 (design-risks v0.13.1-M) + updated v0.13.5 (v0.13.4-A)
# Provenance: no legacy fixture pins unwind-watcher lifetime directly;
#   behavior follows from normal-close persistence (legacy at-control.chk:3-13)
#   plus the tag-cancellation contract (a throw does not stop user-owned tags).
# Covers: a throw crossing a tag scope (unwind pass-through: non-matching
#         unwind over a TAG_SCOPE entry) must run the same teardown
#         OP_POP_TAG runs — leave event fires, member entry unlinks.
#         Pre-v0.13.3 fix: the walker bare-popped the entry — the leave event
#         never fired ("L" missing) and the scope's member watcher LEAKED past
#         the scope (trig() fired it: hits == 1).
#         v0.13.3 post-fix: log is "cL" and hits stays 0 (watcher cascaded
#         at scope teardown — the "leak" is treated as a bug).
#
#         v0.13.5 (v0.13.4-A) BEHAVIORAL UPDATE: user-owned tags (var u = Tag.new())
#         no longer cascade their watchers at scope teardown — the watcher persists
#         until u.stop() (mirroring the utag_destroy guard).  This is the correct
#         semantic: the throw does not cancel the tag u; u is still accessible
#         and the user can call u.stop() to cancel the watcher.
#         Updated post-fix: log is "cL" (leave event still fires — unaffected by
#         the cascade guard) and hits == 1 (watcher survived the throw, fires when
#         trig() sets never=1).  The "L" confirms leave-event teardown runs; the
#         "hits==1" confirms the watcher persists for user-owned tags.
## timeout: 30
## host: run var u = Tag.new()
## host: run var lv = Realm.u.leave()
## host: run Realm.log = ""
## host: run Realm.hits = 0
## host: run Realm.never = 0
## host: run at (Realm.lv?) Realm.log = Realm.log + "L"
## host: run try { Realm.u: { at (Realm.never == 1) Realm.hits = Realm.hits + 1; throw(7) } } catch (var e) { Realm.log = Realm.log + "c" }
## host: run Realm.log
## host: run var trig = function() { Realm.never = 1 }; Realm.trig()
## host: run Realm.hits
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] <event>
[00000000] ""
[00000000] 0
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000000] "c"
[00000000] "cL"
[00000000] 1
[00000000] 1
